* TIMES.jl crafted case demo12_lst (reference/crafted.toml, 8 Nov 2026): demo12_ls/ls.dd plus
* time windows for the load shifting (ACT_TIME; eqactups.vda L127-158, EQ_SLSIFT; M1.3
* change 24), on TIMES_Demo demo12 (etsap-TIMES/TIMES_Demo @ 962db86, CC BY 4.0): in REG1
* load may be advanced by at most 4 hours (LO) and delayed by at most 6 (UP), and is
* balanced within 12 hours (N). ACT_TIME also fills RP_UPR (init_ext.vda L73), which brings
* the hour map of timslice.mod L110-121 (RS_HR, RJ_SL, RS_UP, JS_CCL) used by the MOD
* window terms; eqactups.vda L33 rebuilds RP_UPR from ACT_CSTRMP before the equations, so
* no ramping equation (EQ_ACTRMPC) comes with it.
$ONEMPTY
$ONEPS
$ONWARNING
PARAMETER
ACT_TIME ' '/
REG1.2005.LSCOMELC.LO 4
REG1.2005.LSCOMELC.UP 6
REG1.2005.LSCOMELC.N 12
/
